    <version>1.7.0</version>
    <time>1786304497</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update to 1.7.0

- Add ChatOpenAIMantle for the Bedrock Mantle OpenAI-compatible API
- Support the reasoning_effort parameter for ChatBedrockConverse
- Use Anthropic simplified prompt cache management in ChatBedrockConverse
- Include the model name in invocation_params for Bedrock chat models

1.7.0 adds tests/unit_tests/chat_models/test_openai.py, which drives the new
ChatOpenAIMantle model through the python-langchain-tests ChatModel unit-test
bridge. That bridge is not packaged in Factory, so the module is added to the
existing --ignore list rather than the whole %check being dropped. Note the
langchain-aws[openai] extra itself IS satisfiable (python-langchain-openai
1.4.1 + python-openai 2.45.0); langchain-tests is the only blocker. No runtime
dependency is needed either way -- upstream defers the langchain_openai import
via __getattr__, so ChatOpenAIMantle only pulls it in on attribute access.

Built and verified on aarch64: 545 tests pass on both python313 and python314,
rpmlint 0 errors / 0 warnings / 0 badness, source_validator clean.</comment>
    <requestid>1370149</requestid>
